## Diagnosis of the 2 failures above (UnicodeDecodeError, cp1252)
tests/test_phase3_labels.py reads README.md and docs/TRACEABILITY.md with Path.read_text() and no encoding, so Windows decodes UTF-8 as cp1252.
The undecodable bytes (0x81) come from characters that were in these files before this review: README lines 207, 232, 280-282 ('10⁻⁷', '10⁻⁹', '10⁻¹⁶', '10⁻¹⁰') and TRACEABILITY line 12 ('10⁴-case') and line 18 ('ρ_up'). None is in text added by this review.
Pre-existing Windows portability defect in the test (not fixed: editing a test changes the suite fingerprint and would invalidate every merge file).

